From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lagz0ne <15101444+lagz0ne@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 04:40:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/9] feat(ui): put away the team and product chrome on a
 one-person instance

This doop runs for one person and their agents (sign-up is closed), so the
entry points to everything built for teams and the hosted product are
hidden: workspaces (rail section, "Move to workspace"), "Owned by me" /
"Shared with me", Community, Automations and Integrations (rail, the home
hero's automation chip and its integrations bar), owner/member avatar
stacks on canvas tiles, the plan line in the account menu, Share (canvas
top bar, phone menu, canvas tile menu), the canvas Help menu (docs,
support chat) and the Webhooks settings pane.

Kept on purpose: the presence pill (it is also where a working agent
shows), comments, the Doop Agent, Activity, Memory, Connect AI and Agent
keys (the host's MCP key is one).

Only the ways in are hidden: the pages still open by URL and the server
is unchanged, so none of this is a permission. One flag, FULL_UI in
src/lib/fullUi.ts, guards every spot; localStorage['doop:full-ui'] = 'on'
and a reload bring the full UI back.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
